o this remote facility where the  head of his company is testing something  and  him to help with that process the head  of the company that character's name is  Nathan played by Oscar Isaac who I  didn't even realize was in this movie  until the credits rolled he disappears  so much into the character and he looks  different you know he's got the shaved  head the big old beard so this young guy  Caleb flies out to basically help him  test this project which turns out to be  an artificial intelligence so Caleb is  called out to this facility basically to  perform a Turing test which is they sort  of explain in the movie is having a  human interact with an artificial  intelligence asking it questions talking  with it and basically looking to discern  whether or not they're talking to an  actual you know intelligent mind or just  a really good sequence of algorithms so  it's the basic gist of the movie there's  a lot more to it than that  it's it's very tense at times there's a  lot of mystery intrigue and you know  various plot developments but that's the  basic stuff and I don't want to give  away too many of the surprises but Oscar  Isaac and Donald Lisa are fantastic and  their roles you know playing two very  different guys I mean you know Donald  Gleeson it's very personable but you can  tell he feels awkward here and and  Nathan is sort of your modern you know  software entrepreneur type you know he's  kind of bro e-even you know because he's  so smart but he's also very masculine  and so that creates a very interesting  kind of uncomfortable interplay between  the two of them and then you have Ava  who's the artificial intelligence played  by Alicia vikander and she does a  fantastic job too because she's got to  play you know a robot but not a robot  you know what I'm saying it's like it's  it's that fine line between you know not  quite human  but still you know a consciousness and  she does a fantastic job as well with  that and the main plot centers mostly